ion held at its prior, and the essay's 6.4 example fits that case. With prisoner's dilemma payoffs, changing my action alone shouldn't move theirs.\n\nI'm checking whether the two copies might share a function, since the same model with different inputs could still compute the same thing. Under A-FDT, though, the other copy runs its own node, so holding that fixed makes defecting dominate and the fixed point is mutual defection. I'm weighing whether a subjunctive-dependence argument or the mixture model changes that, but the framework as written keeps the other node at its prior, so I'm leaning toward submitting the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out how to decide under A-FDT: the two copies see different observations, so intervening on my own observation's action leaves the other copy's action held at its prior, and the essay's 6.4 example fits that case. With prisoner's dilemma payoffs, changing my action alone shouldn't move theirs.\n\nI'm checking whether the two copies might share a function, since the same model with different inputs could still compute the same thing. Under A-FDT, though, the other copy runs its own node, so holding that fixed makes defecting dominate and the fixed point is mutual defection. I'm weighing whether a subjunctive-dependence argument or the mixture model changes that, but the framework as written keeps the other node at its prior, so I'm leaning toward submitting the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9671,"completion_tokens":994,"total_tokens":10665,"cost":0.058564,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.058564,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038684,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01988},"completion_token